# Library roots and extra flags passed to exit66jukebox (-root is repeatable).
# Use absolute paths; %h and $HOME are NOT expanded in this file.
# Edit me: absolute path, e.g. -root /home/you/Music
EXIT66_ARGS=-root /path/to/music

# Public origin of this install: scheme and host, no path. REQUIRED unless the
# server listens on loopback -- the default -addr :8066 is a wildcard bind and
# does not count. Without it, invites, password resets, email verification and
# signup all fail with a 503. See the Configuration section of the README.
#EXIT66_PUBLIC_ORIGIN=https://jukebox.example.com

# TOTP enrolment and verification: 32 raw bytes as base64 or hex. Generate with
# openssl rand -base64 32. A malformed value aborts startup; a missing one
# starts fine and fails later with 500 mfa unavailable.
#EXIT66_MFA_KEY=

# Silence the browser's local audio during a Sonos cast (default true):
#EXIT66_MUTE_LOCAL_ON_CAST=true

# Optional OIDC sign-in (all three are needed; any missing one leaves sign-in
# password-only). Register <EXIT66_PUBLIC_ORIGIN>/api/auth/oidc/callback as the
# redirect URI with your provider -- that path is fixed, and a provider set
# without EXIT66_PUBLIC_ORIGIN is disabled at startup. Copy the issuer exactly,
# trailing slash included if your provider publishes one. See the Configuration
# section of the README for the account-linking rules.
#EXIT66_OIDC_ISSUER=
#EXIT66_OIDC_CLIENT_ID=
#EXIT66_OIDC_CLIENT_SECRET=
# What the login screen calls it (default: single sign-on):
#EXIT66_OIDC_NAME=

# Optional outgoing mail (host empty = no email is sent at all). The host alone
# switches SMTP on, so a partial config half-works: the port is never checked,
# an empty user sends unauthenticated rather than disabling the send, and a
# from address your relay rejects still leaves SMTP "on".
#EXIT66_SMTP_HOST=
#EXIT66_SMTP_PORT=587
#EXIT66_SMTP_USER=
#EXIT66_SMTP_PASS=
#EXIT66_SMTP_FROM=

# Optional scrobbling credentials (uncomment + fill). Last.fm needs both key
# and secret, plus a one-time `exit66jukebox lastfm-auth`:
#EXIT66_LISTENBRAINZ_TOKEN=
#EXIT66_LASTFM_API_KEY=
#EXIT66_LASTFM_API_SECRET=

# Federation. These only SEED an install that has never saved federation
# settings -- once they are saved from the admin panel the stored settings win
# and these are ignored. An empty role leaves every other FED variable inert.
# Do not leave a trailing comment on a line you uncomment: systemd keeps it as
# part of the value.
#
# Role is hub, member or peer:
#EXIT66_FED_ROLE=
# Members: the hub's public host:port to dial. Hubs: local listen address,
# e.g. :8443:
#EXIT66_FED_HUB=
#EXIT66_FED_LISTEN=
# Shared secret presented at registration, and this instance's id (e.g. home):
#EXIT66_FED_TOKEN=
#EXIT66_FED_PEER_ID=
# Peers: WebRTC direct transport is on unless this is set to 0:
#EXIT66_FED_DIRECT_P2P=
# Peers: comma-separated STUN URLs (unset uses the built-in default), and a
# TURN URL for when NAT traversal fails:
#EXIT66_FED_STUN=
#EXIT66_FED_TURN=
